# DeskPet Dev Rules (.geminirules)

Adapted from Karpathy Guidelines & DeskPet architecture. ALWAYS follow when editing or debugging.

## Core Principles

1. **Think First**: Surface assumptions and trade-offs before coding. Ask questions if game logic, formulas, or scaling is unclear. Suggest simpler paths. When evaluating an external code review, audit, or plan, verify the active branch (`main` vs `cp/crowley-aziraphale`), commit baseline vs `HEAD`, exact file/line citations, runtime facts (e.g., `process.versions`), missing context, and actual test runs before agreeing or acting—never assume a report is free of stale items or false positives.
2. **Use Skills First**: Before writing code, documentation, or designing architecture, you MUST proactively review your available skills and read the relevant `SKILL.md` via `read_file`:
   - Project skills (`.agents/skills/`): `desktop-pet-maintenance` (renderer/main/IPC/display/skins), `skin-asset-pipeline` (sprites/WebP/encryption), `release-and-packaging` (builds/ASAR/signing/workflows).
   - Global skills: `debugging-and-error-recovery`, `frontend-ui-engineering`, `game-ui-ux`, `code-review-and-quality`, `documentation-and-adrs`, and orchestration skills (`swarm`, `subagent-driven-development`).
3. **Simplicity First**: Write minimum code. Avoid speculative abstractions or premature OOP registry structures.
4. **Surgical Edits**: Modify only lines needed. Match existing style (Vanilla JS, standard CSS). Remove orphaned code created by your edits; do not touch other unrelated code.
5. **Goal-Driven & Chain Verification**: When executing multi-step tasks (`/goal` or multi-bug fixes):
   - Solve exactly ONE problem at a time.
   - After each atomic fix, verify and update corresponding unit tests (`test/`). Prefer behavioral tests (mocks, fake timers, `FakeBrowserWindow`) over regex/source-matching assertions (`assert.match(source, ...)`), except for intentional static security/manifest invariants. Run `npm test` (plus `npm run test:integration` for IPC/service/window lifecycle changes).
   - **Proactive Documentation & Plan Sync**: YOU MUST automatically:
     1. Check off completed items (`- [x]`) in the active `docs/plan/*.md` file immediately upon completing each task/phase, ensuring cross-platform agents (macOS / Windows) stay in sync.
     2. Update `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/structure.md`, and relevant ADRs (`docs/decisions/`) in the same step, with explicit cross-links (`[ADR-xxx](docs/decisions/ADR-xxx.md)`), and verify with `npm run check:adrs` and `node --test test/docLinks.test.js`.
   - **Phase-based Atomic Commits**: For multi-phase plans, create an atomic commit at the end of each completed phase/task together with its tests, plan checkbox updates, and docs to maintain clean bisectability and rollback checkpoints. Provide manual verification steps for security changes or complex refactors.
   - Never batch changes without running intermediate verification and updating docs for each step.

## Technical Constraints

1. **Process Separation & Security**:
   - Main (`main.js`): System tasks, native window management, tray, IPC routes, `electron-store`.
   - Preload (`preload.js`): Safe context bridge via `window.electronAPI`.
   - Renderer (`src/`): Game loop, systems, UI rendering. No direct Node API access.
   - IPC Authorization: Validate all sensitive operations (skin changes, asset loading, filesystem requests) inside main-process IPC handlers (`src/main/services/*`, `src/main/windows/*`, `src/main/DisplayService.js`; channel contracts in `ipcContracts.js`). When restricting sender IDs, retain E2E QA entry points (`app.openSkinSelectorForQA`, `app.openSettingsForQA`).
2. **Game Loop & Time Skew (`src/app.js`)**:
   - Must wrap step iterations in `try/catch` to prevent renderer crashes.
   - Synchronize sprite orientation on transition frame to avoid visual glitches.
   - Sleep/Resume Guard: Clamp or validate time deltas across sleep/wake (e.g., macOS Dark Wake) to prevent erroneous transitions.
   - External API Metrics: Strictly validate numeric fields (e.g., weather coordinates/temperatures) with `firstFiniteNumber` to prevent implicit `Number(null)` -> `0` coercion.
3. **Multi-Display & DPI**:
   - Coordinate conversion via `displayBounds.js`.
   - Window refit/debounce behavior via `displayFit.js`; keep Electron `screen` event coalescing and min/max constraint bridging together.
   - Send renderer `screen-info` only after the main transparent window has settled to the intended virtual desktop bounds.
   - Apply `scaleRatio` to `PetRenderer`, `ContextMenu`, and effects to maintain consistent physical sizing across screens.
4. **macOS vs Windows Window Management & Sub-Window UI**:
   - When modifying `alwaysOnTop` or visibility during fullscreen/space transitions in `main.js` or sub-windows (settings, skin selector, pomodoro), account for macOS space isolation, `skipTransformProcessType: true` on `setVisibleOnAllWorkspaces`, guarded `app.focus({ steal: true })`, `alwaysOnTop` overlay stacking, and fullscreen rearrangement to prevent trapped, hidden, or flickering windows.
   - For sub-window UI or layout changes, verify zero unintended scroll overflow/clipping across `zh`/`en`/`ja` in real Electron (`npm run test:e2e` or Playwright measurement; `test:e2e:ci` only runs the startup, settings window, IPC isolation, and font specs), not just fake-DOM unit tests.
5. **Input & Drag**:
   - Default: `setIgnoreMouseEvents(true, { forward: true })`. Toggle to `false` only on hover of interactive elements.
   - Set `isDragging = true` on drag, pausing `MovementSystem` and `InteractionSystem`.

## Asset Pipeline & Skin System (`src/assets/`, `skinGallery.js`)

1. **Pipeline Adherence**: Strictly follow `docs/skin-pipeline-guide.md` when modifying skins/sprites (`webp` format, `walk_left`/`walk_right` prefixes).
2. **Sync Manifests & Readmes**: Synchronize skin entries across `skinGallery.js`, `protectedAssetLoader.js`, and all three language Readmes (`readme_zh.txt`, `readme_en.txt`, `readme_ja.txt`); when a sub-window loads `pet-asset://` resources, its HTML CSP must allow `pet-asset:`.
3. **Skin Selector State Machine**: Support `isPreview` workflow (preview without committing; cancel safely restores previous skin).

## Browser Support & Web Standards Policy

1. **Runtime & Zero Polyfills**: Target Electron 45+ (Chromium 156+) directly with zero external polyfills, component libraries, or CDN scripts/styles (strict CSP).
2. **Native Web Standards**: Use Popover API (`popover="manual"`), CSS Anchor Positioning, Relative Color Syntax (`rgb(from ...)`), `@starting-style` / `allow-discrete`, `content-visibility: auto` + `contain-intrinsic-size`, standard ARIA semantics (`role="meter"`, `aria-disabled="true"`), and `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`.
3. **Fake-DOM Test Compatibility**: Guard modern web API calls in renderer JS (`showPopover`, `hidePopover`, `getAnimations`) with feature detection or optional chaining (`?.()`) + fallback timers so Node.js fake-DOM tests run cleanly.

## Git Workflow & Versioning

Before commit/push:
1. **Update CHANGELOG.md**: Group under exact headings (`Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`, `Security`) without duplicate headings under the same version. Keep `Unreleased` entries in oldest-to-newest order, written in clear Chinese (except code terms/proper nouns), strictly beneath `## [Unreleased]`, and link ADRs when relevant.
2. **Update docs when behavior changes**: Keep `docs/structure.md`, `docs/git-workflow.md`, `README.md`/`readme_*.txt`, relevant ADRs, and `package-lock.json` (when dependencies/`engines` change) in sync.
3. **Atomic Commits**: Message format: `<type>: <short description>\n\n<body explaining why>`.
4. **Pushing**: Run `./push.sh` (macOS/Linux) or `.\push.ps1` (Windows) early to catch preflight format validation issues. Both reject unstaged untracked files, run `npm run sync:cp -- --verify` on `main`, and accept `[skip-cp]` for `main`-only changes.
